{"content":[{"c":["GOZAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City and district near the Euphrates River. The Habor River (modern Khabur) flowed through it. The Assyrians conquered it sometime before Sennacherib’s invasion of Judah (701 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). This fact is mentioned by Sennacherib, king of Assyria, in a blasphemous letter sent to Hezekiah, king of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.12","r":"2Kgs.19.12","rawR":"2Kgs.19.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.12","value":"2Kgs.19.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.12","r":"Isa.37.12","rawR":"Isa.37.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.12","value":"Isa.37.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 37:12"},"). Later it became one of the places in Assyria where conquered Israelites were deported."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gozan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.12","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.12","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.12"},{"anchorText":"Is 37:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.12","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.12","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"641f4bfaaeac8db5b72253b8c309e09ba300e6962c65743f9be95985667043ba","sourceItemName":"Gozan","sourceItemOrder":197,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Gozan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gozan","title":"Gozan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}